# Out-of-vault secrets file referenced by Obsidian vault notes.
# Copy to ~/.config/claude-memory/secrets.env and chmod 600.
# Source it in your shell (or the relevant tool) before running commands that need the values.
#
# The point of this file: keep API tokens, keys, and other credentials OUT of the vault
# (which is git-tracked and pushed to a remote). Vault notes reference variable names
# only; literal values live here.
#
# Example:
#   export SLACK_USER_TOKEN="xoxp-..."
#   export OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."
#
# After adding a secret here, document the variable name in the relevant Tools/<tool>.md
# note, e.g.:
#   Token: stored in ~/.config/claude-memory/secrets.env as SLACK_USER_TOKEN
